A||N||4||Hippocrat||Switching from 4spd to 5||||6||
Z||000000||Hippocrat||09-11-2001||02:31 AM||||Yes yes .. yet another new comer to the wonderful world of Fieros.. <BR>Quick question.. what considerations have to be made when swapping a 4spd for a 5 .. selector cables etc.. or can you just bolt the 5spd in and go?<BR> thanx..||||reg||6
Z||000001||Standard||09-11-2001||02:55 AM||||you need the master and slave cylinders for the 5 speed, and i believe the shift cables too.<P>And welcome!  You've found the best place on the net for Fiero stuff.  pretty much the best place on the net for anything, really  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">         <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 09-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hippocrat||09-11-2001||03:28 AM||||Thank you .. I got that impression while reading through this forum for the past week or so. Seems to be a lot of helpful and knowledgeable people here. The only thing that seems to be missing is the abnormally large ego factor usually associated with these forums. Think Im going to like it here.<P>again thanks for the tip about the cylinders||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||09-11-2001||07:37 AM||||You need only to replace the slave cylinder. You will also need to replace the prom in the brain box, shifter, clutch and pressure plate. Some wiring modification required for working back up lights.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||09-11-2001||07:53 AM||||You didn't say whether you have a Duke or a V-6, but before you go and spend a bunch of money on a V-6 Fiero 5-speed (Getrag), look at the Isuzu 5 speed which came with the later 4 cylinder cars. Also look at the Beretta/Cavalier version of the Getrag. They are much more common in the recycle yards, and can be adapted fairly cheaply.  Check <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  for bits and pieces.<BR>A lot of folks prefer the Isuzu's gear spacing, anyway. It's weak point is supposed to be the shift forks. Doesn't like being speed shifted. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
